Tex. Civ. Prac. & Rem. Code § 17.042

In addition to other acts that may constitute doing business, a nonresident does business in this state if the nonresident:

(1) contracts by mail or otherwise with a Texas resident and either party is to perform the contract in whole or in part in this state;

(2) commits a tort in whole or in part in this state;

Va. Code Ann. § 8.01-328.1

A. A court may exercise personal jurisdiction over a person, who acts directly or by an agent, as to a cause of action arising from the person's:

1. Transacting any business in this Commonwealth;

3. Causing tortious injury by an act or omission in this Commonwealth;

Wash. Rev. Code § 4.16.080

The following actions shall be commenced within three years:

(2) An action for taking, detaining, or injuring personal property, including an action for the specific recovery thereof, or for any other injury to the person or rights of another not hereinafter enumerated;

735 ILCS 5/2-209

(a) Any person, whether or not a citizen or resident of this State, who in person or through an agent does any of the acts hereinafter enumerated, thereby submits such person to the jurisdiction of the courts of this State as to any cause of action arising from:

(1) The transaction of any business within this State;

(2) The commission of a tortious act within this State;
